      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before settlers, the area along Contentnea Creek that became Stantonsburg was inhabited by Native Americans until about 1720.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofstantonsburg.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Main Street hosts a historic post office, a library, and an elementary school, reflecting the town’s long‑standing community focus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofstantonsburg.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town park offers a walking trail, soccer nets, basketball goals, and a covered picnic area with bathrooms for visitors.",
